    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d962">

                <pb facs="1103" n="1023" xml:id="pg1023"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Hay to Mr. Leishman.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1902-05-08"><hi rendition="#italic">May 8,
                        1902</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 153.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have to acknowledge the receipt of your
                    dispatch, No. 143, of March 1 last, on the subject of the abduction of Miss
                    Stone.</p>
                <p>You will express the grateful appreciation of the Presidents and myself to the
                    persons mentioned in your dispatch for their generous and valuable services in
                    connection with the release of Miss Stone.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">John Hay.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
